title: $:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-ironworks/screws
tags: [[$:/tags/Stylesheet]]
code-body: yes

<!--
Screw angles.

Nobody drives four screws to the same angle, and nobody drives the screws in
two panels to the same angles either. base.tid draws the heads and the slots;
this file is the only thing that decides which way each slot points.

It lives in its own stylesheet tiddler because it needs a widget: base.tid
restricts wikitext parsing with `\rules only` and cannot contain a list. The
same constraint put the sticky-title z-index ladder in sticky.tid.

CSS has no random(). What it has is arithmetic and a position in a list, and
that is enough: the angle for corner c of tiddler n is (n x step + offset) mod
180, with a different step per corner. Steps that share no factor with the
cycle length walk the whole range instead of falling into a short pattern, so
the four screws in one plate disagree with each other, and the plate below
disagrees with both.

Deterministic, which is better than random here: a tiddler's screws do not
twitch to new angles when it re-renders, and two people looking at the same
wiki are looking at the same plate.

The modulus is 180 rather than 360 because a slot has no top: turning one
through half a circle gives back the slot you started with, and asking for
angles in the range 180-360 would only repeat the first half.

17 rules, so the cycle is long enough that a reader would have to count down a
river of 18 tiddlers to catch it repeating. Vanilla's own ladder settled on
100 rules for the same kind of trick; 17 is plenty for something this quiet.

Note the quoting, because getting it wrong is silent and expensive. The CSS
fragments are wrapped in SINGLE backticks, inside the list, so that the widgets
between them stay live. Wrapping the whole block in double backticks instead —
which is what this file did at first — turns the $list and every $text into
literal text: the widget markup lands in the stylesheet verbatim, and the CSS
parser then throws away the rule that follows it. See sticky.tid, which uses
the same escape and closes its code span BEFORE its list starts.
-->

<$list filter="[range[17]]" variable="n">
`.iw-screws .tc-story-river .tc-tiddler-frame:nth-child(17n+`<$text text=<<n>>/>`)::before {
	--iw-screw-a1: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[41]add[13]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a2: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[67]add[52]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a3: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[97]add[31]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a4: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[113]add[74]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
}

.iw-screws .tc-story-river .tc-live-reorderable:nth-child(17n+`<$text text=<<n>>/>`) .tc-tiddler-frame::before {
	--iw-screw-a1: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[41]add[13]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a2: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[67]add[52]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a3: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[97]add[31]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
	--iw-screw-a4: `<$text text={{{ [<n>multiply[113]add[74]remainder[180]] }}}/>`deg;
}`
</$list>

`.iw-screws .tc-story-river .tc-tiddler-frame::before {

	--iw-screw-slot-1: linear-gradient(
		calc(var(--iw-screw-a1) + 90deg),
		transparent calc(50% - 1.5px),
		var(--iw-screw-wall) calc(50% - 1.5px) calc(50% - 0.8px),
		var(--iw-screw-slot-ink) calc(50% - 0.8px) calc(50% + 1px),
		transparent calc(50% + 1px)
	);
	--iw-screw-slot-2: linear-gradient(
		calc(var(--iw-screw-a2) + 90deg),
		transparent calc(50% - 1.5px),
		var(--iw-screw-wall) calc(50% - 1.5px) calc(50% - 0.8px),
		var(--iw-screw-slot-ink) calc(50% - 0.8px) calc(50% + 1px),
		transparent calc(50% + 1px)
	);
	--iw-screw-slot-3: linear-gradient(
		calc(var(--iw-screw-a3) + 90deg),
		transparent calc(50% - 1.5px),
		var(--iw-screw-wall) calc(50% - 1.5px) calc(50% - 0.8px),
		var(--iw-screw-slot-ink) calc(50% - 0.8px) calc(50% + 1px),
		transparent calc(50% + 1px)
	);
	--iw-screw-slot-4: linear-gradient(
		calc(var(--iw-screw-a4) + 90deg),
		transparent calc(50% - 1.5px),
		var(--iw-screw-wall) calc(50% - 1.5px) calc(50% - 0.8px),
		var(--iw-screw-slot-ink) calc(50% - 0.8px) calc(50% + 1px),
		transparent calc(50% + 1px)
	);

}`
